02:46.760 --> 02:53.700
If anyone's unfamiliar with stage analysis, this is a 30 week moving average on a weekly time frame.

02:54.220 --> 03:00.920
Stage one is when we build a base and a characteristic of that base is we oscillate above and below the 30 week moving average.

03:00.920 --> 03:10.300
Then we get the markup campaign, also known as stage two, where you will see price moves above the 30 weekly and uses it as support or trades above it.

03:10.580 --> 03:14.360
And another key characteristic of stage two is the 30 week turns up.

03:14.680 --> 03:23.740
Then we get stage three, the top, which again, we tend to oscillate up and down, above and below the 30 week as the 30 week rolls over and starts to point down.

03:23.740 --> 03:33.760
And then stage four, we tend to do the opposite to stage two, okay, and use that downward slope instead of the upward slope in 30 week moving average as resistance instead of support.

03:33.900 --> 03:35.700
And then we enter stage one again.

03:35.920 --> 03:41.680
And if an asset has another cycle of bullishness in it, then of course it will emerge from stage one to stage two again.

03:41.900 --> 03:44.140
